en got their own  sitcom penny Marshall's Laverne was edgy  Cindy Williams Shirley was a bit more  optimistic they were roommates best  friends and co-workers at the shots  brewery in the late 50s and early 60s  bubbling with energy Laverne and Shirley  balanced their time at the bottling  plant while hanging out at laverne's  father's restaurant and fending off the  advances of their nerdy and obnoxious  friends 1980 1983 1992 to 1994 60  minutes 60 minutes has been a part of  the CBS lineup since 1968 and the show's  in-depth reporting made it a pioneer in  TV news it's produced a few moments of  world-changing journalism such as Mike  Wallace's 1996 story about tobacco  industry whistleblower Jeffrey wagon  but perhaps 60 minutes most famous  segment has been the show ending palate  cleanser a few minutes with Andy Rooney  in which the veteran humorously  complained about whatever he felt like  but not sleeping is not my problem  Justin Bieber Lady Gaga and Usher I mean  who when did bright colored plastic cows  pigs and rabbits get to be art I don't  like most of the stuff passing for art  and it's everywhere 1981 1982 and 1984  Dallas primetime soaps were the biggest  TV fad in the late 70s and early 80s and  the biggest of the ball was Dallas it  centered around the Ewing family and  their massive Texas based oil company  headed by Larry hagman's downright evil  jr. Ewing it also produced one of the  most watched TV events ever the two-part  who shot jr. cliffhanger that got people  tuning in the following season 1985  dynasty by 1985 the popularity of Dallas  had diminished but audiences still  wanted to see rich people behaving badly  on prime-time television ABC happily  obliged with dynasty starring John  Forsythe as tycoon Blake Carrington ad  in a much younger secretary turned wife  as well as Joan Collins as Blake's  ex-wife Alexis and the show discovered  exactly what people wanted to see Alexis  and her new rival  getting into arguments then slapping  each other while wearing extremely  expensive clothes 1986 to 1990 The Cosby  Show with the recent allegations against  Bill Cosby it's easy to forget his show  was once so well-loved debuting on NBC  in 1984 when the popularity of sitcoms  was fading The Cosby Show was crafted to  be a groundbreaking portrayal of a black  family something that was rarely seen on  TV The Cosby Show often played fast and  loose with sitcom standards and in doing  so changed viewers expectations some  episodes tackled heavy subject matter  while others had almost no plot at all  and just featured the family hanging out  and showing how great it was for a  family to be together it all came  together to make The Cosby Show an  unstoppable juggernaut 1990 Roseanne The  Cosby Show wasn't alone as the most  viewed show on TV in 1990 it also had to  contend with Roseanne another show that  broke new ground in television  representation rarely had anyone  attempted a show about a blue-collar  Midwestern family with two working  parents but Roseanne was also the anti  Cosby Show built around a family with  financial struggles messy lives and real  world problems that never resolved at  the end of an episode through it all  they still managed to stay a close-knit  family it was such an indelible portrait  of this particular kind of American  family that ABC revived Roseanne for a  short-lived 2018 run more than 20 years  after it initially went off the air 1991  cheers cheers was so different from  other contemporary sitcoms when it  debuted in 1982 it was nearly canceled  before taking home some Emmys in 1983 by  1989 everyone was invested in what  became the nation's favorite  neighborhood bar and the cast of  characters who frequented it it was so  popular in fact that it led to the also  successful spin-off Frasier launched the  career of Woody Harrelson and gets a  shout out in scores of pop-culture  references 1995 and 1998 Seinfeld  finally after years of shows about  things along came a show about nothing  except that Seinfeld was about something  the hilariously dark and selfish  impulses of some nasty New Yorkers based  on Jerry Seinfeld's scattered  observational comedy it turned into one  of the most intricately written and  inventive sitcoms ever made  it also upended the traditional sitcom  formula by featuring bizarre classic  moments like ordering from The Soup Nazi  and messing up an operation by dropping  a Junior Mints  Americans love the cleverly written  storylines that somehow all connected at  the end and it beat everything else on  the air 1996 to 1997 and 1999 er the  fast paced ultra realistic drama ER  marked another shift in viewer tastes  breaking up the life and death tension  of a big-city emergency room were scenes  involving the doctor's personal lives  moments that were just as captivating  thanks to stars like George Clooney  julianna margulies and Noah Wyle ER was  a mainstay of NBC scheduled for 15  seasons and at times it was the  most-watched show on TV  [Music]
 

